{
	"_comment": [
		"Per-hotspot walk targets. The render_model export stores a walk nav's walk_to",
		"and arrive_at once per DESTINATION LABEL, not per hotspot: across all 90",
		"movies no label carries two distinct pairs. Every exit leading to the same",
		"room therefore reuses one room's coordinates, so Piposh walks away from the",
		"hotspot that was clicked and then enters the next room on the wrong side.",
		"",
		"Recovered from the export itself, using the original's own model: a doorway is",
		"a place. The spot Piposh walks to in room S on his way to room D is the same",
		"spot he stands on when he arrives in S from D. The surviving pair for label T",
		"is one edge's doorway pair -- walk_to(T) is the doorway in T's canonical",
		"source room, arrive_at(T) the doorway in T facing it -- so identifying that",
		"source room fills both directions of that edge and re-derives its other",
		"hotspots. tools/rebuild_doorways.py regenerates this file.",
		"",
		"Covers 154 of 212 same-movie walk hotspots: 116 already carried the right",
		"values, 38 are corrected here. The remaining 58 are mostly HOTEL1 and AIR1,",
		"whose transition destinations are still in unmapped_transitions and so have no",
		"reverse edge to read. They keep the exported values and stay wrong.",
		"",
		"Key: \"<room>|<channel>|<target_label>\", room lowercased with any 'go' suffix",
		"stripped (MovieContext._room_key), matching the marker under the playhead.",
		"NOT under assets/ on purpose: that tree is mirrored with robocopy /MIR."
	],
